<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>opening day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Glamorgan 272-9 (R.Croft 81, M.Maynard 59;</p>
<p>A.Fraser 4-67) v Middlesex.</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey 426-6 (A.Stewart 200 not out,</p>
<p>A.Hollioake 69, B.Hollioake 53) v Yorkshire.</p>
<p>At Bristol: Worcestershire 243-8 (S.Rhodes 78, K.Spiring 52,</p>
<p>S.Lampitt 51 not out) v Gloucestershire.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Derbyshire 200 (V.Clarke 99; N.Smith 4-37;</p>
<p>D.Brown 4-33). Warwickshire 4-0.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Kent 151-5 v Lancashire.</p>
<p>At Basingstoke: Hampshire 204. Somerset 79-6.</p>
<p>At Hove: Sussex 140 (A.Cowan 5-45; N.Williams 4-29). Essex</p>
<p>232-5 (R.Irani 79 not out).</p>
